      "path": "cordis.patch.yml",
      "content": "# dsh-web-tools — Host plugin patch layer\n#\n# - Re-enables the DSH native model-facing web tools (web_search / web_fetch),\n#   which the web-app bundle disables by default.\n# - The `tool-web` row is a full config replacement: DSH patch semantics assign\n#   `config` as a whole object (no per-key deep merge), so every base key must\n#   be restated here or it falls back to the plugin default.\n#   In particular `fetch: true` is what actually registers the `web_fetch`\n#   tool schema and its system-prompt guidance — without it the model never\n#   sees web_fetch at all, no matter what providers are registered.\n# - Points ctx.web at the dsh-web-tools providers so both seams execute\n#   through our multi-provider pool instead of the bundled DeepSeek search.\n- id: tool-web\n  disabled: false\n  config:\n    search: true\n    fetch: true\n    searchMaxQueries: 4\n    searchMaxResults: 8\n    searchTimeoutMs: 60000\n    fetchTimeoutMs: 30000\n    fetchMaxOutputChars: 200000\n\n- id: web\n  config:\n    searchProvider: dsh-web-tools\n    fetchProvider: dsh-web-tools-fetch\n\n- insert:\n    - id: dsh-web-tools\n      name: 'dsh-web-tools'\n"
